        "procedure": "Shared procedure: lanthanide nitrate (0.2 mmol) in absolute ethanol (5 cm3) was added dropwise to L (0.2 mmol) in absolute ethanol, stirred at room temperature for 4 h. The white powder was redissolved in 1:1 CH3OH/CHCl3; crystals of 1 suitable for X-ray diffraction formed after evaporation for several months. Ligand L was prepared separately from triethanolamine, NaH, and α-chloro-N,N-diethylacetamide in THF.",
